@@ -3,3 +3,10 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a value from a JSON document using an
+[RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). An empty pointer selects the
+whole document. Non-empty pointers must begin with `/`; `~0` represents `~` and `~1` represents
+`/`. The function throws when the pointer is malformed or does not identify a value.
